From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:42:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 117/121] test(refinery): fail loudly when the merge-lane rig
 is not built (gcp-l8td.4)

A self-review touch-up. build_rig runs its git setup quietly, so a setup
that broke (for example a host git that refuses a flag) used to show up
only as confusing lane failures further down. Such a case never passed
vacuously, but it did not name the cause. build_rig now fails the case
with a "harness bug" message when it leaves no temp branch or no
origin/integration behind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh b/gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh
index 2eeb982b..9a0fb7d6 100644
--- a/gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh
+++ b/gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh
@@ -471,8 +471,11 @@ build_rig() {
     # What the `rebase` step leaves behind, including its "skipped previously
     # applied commit" collapse.
     git_q -C "$REFINERY" rebase origin/integration || git_q -C "$REFINERY" rebase --abort
-    TEMP_SHA=$(git -C "$REFINERY" rev-parse temp)
+    TEMP_SHA=$(git -C "$REFINERY" rev-parse --verify -q temp)
     TARGET_BEFORE=$(origin_tip)
+    # The setup above is quiet, so say so plainly when it did not produce a rig.
+    [ -n "$TEMP_SHA" ] && [ -n "$TARGET_BEFORE" ] ||
+        fail "harness bug: build_rig $shape left no temp branch or no origin/integration"
 }
 
 # add_second_worktree — the target branch checked out in another worktree of
